((date 2026-11-12) (slug prebreakout-floor-screen)
 (hypothesis
  "Follow-up of the entry-timing screen, from the DIS/TWX1/SFAM chart walk: the code's support floor (Window_extreme, 8 %) is the dip AFTER the 90-day high, so post-breakout screens anchor the stop on a dip inside the run and clean breakouts skip as No_structural_stop. Does the book-literal floor (book section 5.1: the lowest low of the M weeks before the latest close above the prior N-week high, x 0.96, with the record's 15 % Drop_over_max gate) improve realised NAV-% on the record's entries (5 seeds, N in {8,13,26} x M in {2,4,8}), and do the k0 skips it converts into tickets carry a better payoff? Proxy screen: may conclude only build or no-build.")
 (base_scenario
  "entry-timing-screen-2026-11-12 run.sh step 4: host awk per-trade replay over record-kseed-2026-10-27 k0-k4; entries re-stopped (exit = actual exit unless the book stop hits first; after an initial-stop exit hold until the book stop or 13 weeks) or dropped by the gate; k0 No_structural_stop skips (13,849 first-of-run events) as stop-limit tickets with a 26-week proxy hold, calibrated on the run's own entries (+245 vs +260 NAV-% realised)")
 (window_id top3000-pitv12-2000-2026-record-kseed5-trades) (baseline_label record-kseed-actual)
 (variants
  (((label F1-gate15-n13m4) (config_hash floor-screen-f1-gate15) (aggregate ()))
   ((label F1-nogate-risk-sized-n13m4) (config_hash floor-screen-f1-nogate) (aggregate ()))))
 (verdict Reject)
 (notes
  "NO-BUILD (proxy screen; leans on edge-is-the-fat-tail and the 07-12 entry-shape no-build). Gate on: -101..-261 NAV-% in every cell and seed; 443 of 545 k0 trades dropped at N=13 M=4, incl. 6 of the 8 doubling trades in k0's replayed set (APPS 47 %, BBWI 47 %, MMYT 27 %, AVGO 24 %, LGND 29 %, BGO 36 % book stop distance; k0's ninth doubler, ADSK 2003, fails the basis check and is not replayed). Gate off, risk-sized: -40..-138. Gate off at the run's position size: +58..+81 (5/5) but 173-184 trades worse vs 158-167 better, carried by STRP 2017 (bidding war, +24.1 k0) and GME 2020 (+13.0); deeper stops enlarge losers (FMI 2015 -1.1 -> -7.4, PYX 2018 -1.9 -> -6.7, SIRI 2023 -1.7 -> -6.0, CVNA 2025-12) and put about 2.4 % of NAV at risk per trade on average vs the record's 1 %, >= 5 % on 22 of k0's 524 trades with a book stop (results/sizing.txt: value_over_nav in replay-k0.csv x n13m4_stop_dist in floor.csv; seeds k1-k4 2.40-2.43 % mean, 20-24 trades >= 5 %); the FMI/PYX/SIRI losses are that tail. k0 conversions: 1,264 fills, mean +0.41 vs the run's entries +0.44, median +0.36 vs -0.70, losers 40 % vs 59 %, >= +5 NAV-% trades 0.8 vs 4.7 per 100. WHY: the post-breakout floor is what lets the code buy extended leaders at all; book floor + 15 % gate points the same way as skip-extended (H1) but cuts much deeper (81 % of k0's trades dropped vs about 18 % for H1 at X = 20 %). Writeup dev/experiments/entry-timing-screen-2026-11-12/README.md section F1."))
